WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.091 --> 00:00:01.390
- All right, everybody.

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.331
We are back, kicking things
off in New York City,

00:00:03.331 --> 00:00:05.780
as we celebrate the start of season four.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.072
We have the cast of

00:00:07.072 --> 00:00:09.250
The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.352
in our audience.

00:00:10.352 --> 00:00:11.185
(audience cheering)

00:00:11.185 --> 00:00:12.192
Give it up.

00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:15.712
Already enjoying some snacks
that New York has to offer.

00:00:15.712 --> 00:00:16.872
New York is one of,

00:00:16.872 --> 00:00:19.621
if not the best food cities in the world.

00:00:19.621 --> 00:00:21.570
And I've tried a lot of
it, 'cause I love it.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.179
There's food everywhere
here, it's awesome.

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:25.072
Last year, Amber Ruffin brought me pizza

00:00:25.072 --> 00:00:26.838
from Amore on 58th.

00:00:26.838 --> 00:00:29.760
Mikey Cole brought me
"Mikey likes It" ice cream

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.593
in Hell's Kitchen,

00:00:30.593 --> 00:00:31.712
made a special flavor for me.

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:33.571
It was the KC Masterpiece.

00:00:33.571 --> 00:00:34.752
It was really good.

00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:36.832
And it was rude not to
try again and again.

00:00:36.832 --> 00:00:37.665
(audience laughs)

00:00:37.665 --> 00:00:38.498
(chuckle)

00:00:38.498 --> 00:00:41.073
And the brothers from
Zaro Brothers in the Bronx

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:42.744
hooked me up with some
of their mouthwatering

00:00:42.744 --> 00:00:43.872
black and white cookies.

00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:45.104
Those were outstanding.

00:00:45.104 --> 00:00:47.642
But there are still so
many good eats in New York

00:00:47.642 --> 00:00:48.573
I don't know about.

00:00:48.573 --> 00:00:49.693
There's so many like boroughs

00:00:49.693 --> 00:00:50.771
that have different things going on.

00:00:50.771 --> 00:00:53.002
So here, to share the
foods of her New York,

00:00:53.002 --> 00:00:56.131
please welcome Food Network
Chef, Alex Guarnaschelli.

00:00:56.131 --> 00:00:57.561
(audience applause)

00:00:57.561 --> 00:00:58.394
Guarnaschelli.

00:00:58.394 --> 00:00:59.227
- You did so good there.

00:00:59.227 --> 00:01:00.060
- I like that name. Guarnaschelli.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.893
- Doesn't it sound like a--

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.550
- I'm just gonna keep saying your name.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:04.383
- Yeah, it sounds--

00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:05.277
- It's such a cooler name than mine.

00:01:05.277 --> 00:01:06.358
It's nice to meet you.

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:07.398
- It's nice to meet you.

00:01:07.398 --> 00:01:08.496
It should be a dish, right?

00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:10.665
Like "I'll have the Guarnaschelli
with extra mozzarella"

00:01:10.665 --> 00:01:11.515
or something.

00:01:11.515 --> 00:01:12.348
- Is it a special somewhere?

00:01:12.348 --> 00:01:13.617
Can we make this happen?

00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:15.217
- No, but I think if you have an ice cream

00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:16.887
then maybe I should have like a lasagna.

00:01:16.887 --> 00:01:17.720
- Guarnaschelli.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:18.553
- We should have a meal.

00:01:18.553 --> 00:01:19.386
We should make like a meal together.

00:01:19.386 --> 00:01:20.776
- I will have the Guarnaschelli
with the KC Masterpiece.

00:01:20.776 --> 00:01:21.609
- I like that.

00:01:21.609 --> 00:01:22.442
- It sounds nice.

00:01:22.442 --> 00:01:23.275
I think it rolls off the tongue.

00:01:23.275 --> 00:01:24.108
- I agree.

00:01:24.108 --> 00:01:25.316
- What did you bring us today?

00:01:25.316 --> 00:01:26.506
'Cause I'm smelling it.

00:01:26.506 --> 00:01:27.555
- Yeah, I know. Right?

00:01:27.555 --> 00:01:28.708
It's like, what did you bring us?

00:01:28.708 --> 00:01:29.541
And then we just look.

00:01:29.541 --> 00:01:31.807
So we start here with The
Donut Pub on 14th street.

00:01:31.807 --> 00:01:32.640
- Yes.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.247
- Now they're open really
early in the morning

00:01:34.247 --> 00:01:36.036
and really late at night,
if you know what I mean.

00:01:36.036 --> 00:01:38.447
So those times when like
normal people are sleeping,

00:01:38.447 --> 00:01:39.788
I'm down there buying donuts.

00:01:39.788 --> 00:01:40.621
- Yeah.

00:01:40.621 --> 00:01:41.454
- They know me in there.

00:01:41.454 --> 00:01:42.492
I come in, they're like, "Oh Hey."

00:01:42.492 --> 00:01:44.006
And they just, they get the box out

00:01:44.006 --> 00:01:45.446
and they start loading, you know?

00:01:45.446 --> 00:01:46.694
- Right. And it's super fresh.

00:01:46.694 --> 00:01:47.527
- Yeah. All the time.

00:01:47.527 --> 00:01:48.985
And they're just like

00:01:48.985 --> 00:01:50.014
the formica counter,

00:01:50.014 --> 00:01:52.434
the coffee with too much cream in it.

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.835
And five-- I mean one donut-

00:01:54.835 --> 00:01:55.668
- Yeah.

00:01:55.668 --> 00:01:56.501
- is perfect.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:57.334
(laughs)

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.235
- Wait, I'm gonna feel
rude if I don't try.

00:01:59.235 --> 00:02:00.680
- Yeah. It would really
be very impolite of you.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.591
So, I picked my favorite,
which is the cinnamon cruller.

00:02:02.591 --> 00:02:03.424
- Wait what should I have?

00:02:03.424 --> 00:02:04.257
- No, no.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.090
- Okay.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:05.923
- Get into that girl.

00:02:05.923 --> 00:02:06.756
- Okay.

00:02:06.756 --> 00:02:07.589
- Cheers.

00:02:07.589 --> 00:02:08.422
- Fine.

00:02:08.422 --> 00:02:09.255
- Donut cheers.

00:02:09.255 --> 00:02:10.088
- We're nailing it. (laughs)

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:10.921
- Yeah we're crushing it, really.

00:02:10.921 --> 00:02:11.754
Isn't... Yeah.

00:02:11.754 --> 00:02:12.912
- I love chocolate so much.

00:02:12.912 --> 00:02:13.745
- No I know.

00:02:13.745 --> 00:02:14.578
- Oh my God.

00:02:14.578 --> 00:02:15.411
That's really good.

00:02:15.411 --> 00:02:16.244
- Mmm.

00:02:16.244 --> 00:02:17.712
- What's next? What's happening here?

00:02:17.712 --> 00:02:19.992
- So this is the Nom Wah
Tea Parlor in Chinatown.

00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:21.523
They're over a hundred years old.

00:02:21.523 --> 00:02:22.356
- [Kelly} Yeah.

00:02:22.356 --> 00:02:23.472
- [Alex} It's a dim sum parlor.

00:02:23.472 --> 00:02:24.305
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:24.305 --> 00:02:25.138
- [Alex] But they have,

00:02:25.138 --> 00:02:26.224
this is an egg roll
called the OG egg roll.

00:02:26.224 --> 00:02:27.272
You just dunk and go.

00:02:27.272 --> 00:02:29.752
And then soup dumplings
and shrimp dumplings.

00:02:29.752 --> 00:02:31.843
These are like, this is
like a little planet.

00:02:31.843 --> 00:02:32.676
Look at them.

00:02:32.676 --> 00:02:33.790
They're watching us eat dumplings.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.174
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:35.174 --> 00:02:36.944
- Wait, are we doing these?

00:02:36.944 --> 00:02:37.777
Okay. No, we're doing these.

00:02:37.777 --> 00:02:38.712
- No, we can do whatever.

00:02:38.712 --> 00:02:39.545
- No, you can (indistinct)

00:02:39.545 --> 00:02:40.378
I'm bringing my chopsticks too.

00:02:40.378 --> 00:02:41.211
Whatever.

00:02:41.211 --> 00:02:42.044
(Alex laughs)

00:02:42.044 --> 00:02:43.283
Wait, do you just stick
the whole thing in?

00:02:43.283 --> 00:02:44.116
- I mean quite-

00:02:44.116 --> 00:02:46.592
I mean yes, this is daytime
TV, but let's do it.

00:02:46.592 --> 00:02:48.192
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:48.192 --> 00:02:49.054
Do you like that?

00:02:49.054 --> 00:02:49.887
Sorry.

00:02:51.192 --> 00:02:53.895
- I love you so much. Sorry.

00:02:53.895 --> 00:02:54.795
- Good, right?

00:02:54.795 --> 00:02:55.628
Meaty.

00:02:55.628 --> 00:02:56.545
- What is that?

00:02:56.545 --> 00:02:57.378
- I know, right?

00:02:57.378 --> 00:02:58.566
- That's really good.

00:02:58.566 --> 00:03:01.025
- It's pork with like a
soupy mixture on the outside.

00:03:01.025 --> 00:03:01.858
I know isn't this all-

00:03:01.858 --> 00:03:02.691
I'm gonna stop.

00:03:02.691 --> 00:03:03.705
- Pork is probably my favorite.

00:03:03.705 --> 00:03:04.715
- Yeah, me too.

00:03:04.715 --> 00:03:05.743
And speaking of which,

00:03:05.743 --> 00:03:07.795
this is from my restaurant
Butter in Midtown.

00:03:07.795 --> 00:03:08.628
- Okay.

00:03:08.628 --> 00:03:10.723
- [Alex] This is my pork chop from Butter

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.766
that accidentally became
our signature dish.

00:03:12.766 --> 00:03:14.486
We smoked the racks a little bit,

00:03:14.486 --> 00:03:16.485
and then we grill and broil them.

00:03:16.485 --> 00:03:18.884
And we just started serving
this a few years ago.

00:03:18.884 --> 00:03:19.717
- Yeah.

00:03:19.717 --> 00:03:21.465
- And we were like, you
know, it's a pork chop.

00:03:21.465 --> 00:03:24.566
And people were like, don't
take this off the menu ever.

00:03:24.566 --> 00:03:25.606
We had a couple come in.

00:03:25.606 --> 00:03:26.873
We didn't have some, one night.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.377
They got up and they were like,

00:03:28.377 --> 00:03:29.326
you tell her,

00:03:29.326 --> 00:03:30.846
when she's ready to serve the pork chop,

00:03:30.846 --> 00:03:31.980
we'll be back.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:32.957
(audience laughter)

00:03:32.957 --> 00:03:33.790
- I'm like-

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.026
- It was kind of like a The
Lord of the ring's threat.

00:03:35.026 --> 00:03:36.666
I was like, alright, I
don't know what to do.

00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:37.597
- Wait, now I wanna try it.

00:03:37.597 --> 00:03:38.430
- Yes, dig in.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.263
- Okay, I'm gonna try it.

00:03:39.263 --> 00:03:40.526
- So I cut some on a board
here for you to take.

00:03:40.526 --> 00:03:41.359
- Thank you.

00:03:41.359 --> 00:03:42.448
- It has some sweet potatoes underneath

00:03:42.448 --> 00:03:43.728
and sweet potato chips.

00:03:43.728 --> 00:03:44.666
- [Kelly] I love sweet potatoes.

00:03:44.666 --> 00:03:46.088
- [Alex] I do too.

00:03:46.088 --> 00:03:46.921
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:46.921 --> 00:03:47.754
- [Alex] Really.

00:03:47.754 --> 00:03:48.808
- That wasn't a big enough bite.

00:03:48.808 --> 00:03:50.696
Oh my God. Look how that breaks apart.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:53.008
- [Alex] By the way, they always
said to me on Food Network,

00:03:53.008 --> 00:03:54.696
take little girl bites.

00:03:54.696 --> 00:03:55.529
Will you Alex?

00:03:55.529 --> 00:03:56.362
- Why?

00:03:56.362 --> 00:03:57.195
- Let's do that again.

00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:58.028
Because I-

00:03:58.028 --> 00:03:58.905
- Oh, cause you're eating
a lot of food or something?

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.536
- No, I would just take a really big bite.

00:04:00.536 --> 00:04:01.976
And they're like for the
camera and everything

00:04:01.976 --> 00:04:02.809
for the folks at home,

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.517
maybe dial it back a little bit, Alex.

00:04:04.517 --> 00:04:05.350
(audience laughter)

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:06.183
- You're welcome folks at home.

00:04:06.183 --> 00:04:07.016
It was a mouthful.

00:04:07.016 --> 00:04:08.449
a few times over.

00:04:08.449 --> 00:04:10.015
(audience claps and cheers)

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:11.418
I don't care.

00:04:11.418 --> 00:04:13.389
Thank you so much. That's delicious.

00:04:13.389 --> 00:04:14.509
You can see Alex-

00:04:14.509 --> 00:04:16.479
Literally, she has more jobs than I do,

00:04:16.479 --> 00:04:18.629
all over Food Network.

00:04:18.629 --> 00:04:20.450
Listen, Alex Vs. America,

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.283
Chopped,

00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:22.116
The Kitchen,

00:04:22.116 --> 00:04:23.279
and Supermarket Stakeout.

00:04:23.279 --> 00:04:24.330
You are busy.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.163
(audience cheers)

00:04:25.163 --> 00:04:25.996
Are you tired?

00:04:25.996 --> 00:04:26.829
Do you need the rest?

00:04:26.829 --> 00:04:27.662
- I do.

00:04:27.662 --> 00:04:29.029
I'm actually gonna just move
in here and start cooking.

00:04:29.029 --> 00:04:30.629
- Just move in. Just lay down.

00:04:30.629 --> 00:04:31.599
Literally, you got more jobs than I do.

